                    <p>In production, replace localhost URLs with your Gateway and Identity domains:</p>

                    <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded"><code># Instead of localhost:5075 (Identity) and localhost:5000 (Gateway)
IDENTITY_URL=https://auth.dotnetniger.com
GATEWAY_URL=https://gateway.dotnetniger.com</code></pre>

                    <p class="mt-3">Configure these URLs in <code>appsettings.json</code> via environment variables:</p>

                    <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded"><code># Example .env file for Docker / server
DeveloperPortal__GatewayBaseUrl=https://gateway.dotnetniger.com
Identity__BaseUrl=https://auth.dotnetniger.com

# For API calls, always use the production domain:
curl -X GET https://gateway.dotnetniger.com/ext/my-service/health \
  -H "X-API-Key: dn_your_prod_key"</code></pre>

                    <h6 class="mt-3">Recommendations</h6>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>HTTPS</strong> — Enable TLS on the Gateway and Identity. Use <code>RequireHttpsMetadata = true</code></li>
                        <li><strong>API Keys</strong> — Generate separate production keys. Never reuse development keys</li>
                        <li><strong>Rate limiting</strong> — Adjust limits via <code>RateLimiting:PermitLimit</code> and <code>RateLimiting:WindowSeconds</code></li>
                        <li><strong>OIDC Certificates</strong> — In production, use real certificates (via <code>OpenIddict:CertificatePath</code>) instead of ephemeral dev keys</li>
                        <li><strong>Logs</strong> — Monitor Gateway errors via <code>logs/gateway-*.log</code></li>
                    </ul>
